      "content": "thanks, that helps. but i'm still a bit stuck on the \"objectivity\" part. if conrad is just using the language of the time to be \"accurate,\" doesn't that basically mean the book is just absorbing the racism of the era rather than fighting it? like, if the narrative voice itself stays mostly neutral while describing the natives as \"savages\" or \"primitive,\" isn't that effectively validating those views as just being \"the way things were\"? i'm worried my students might walk away thinking the racism is just a neutral backdrop of history rather than something the book is actually condemning.",
